# Facebook likejacking (2010). A "Play" button that was really a hidden Like, spreading the scam to friends. The social network here is a fictional stand-in.
# A quest (QUESTS.md): the trainee thanks customer posts for a small shop, does one safely, then meets likejacking in a friend's video link.
# The victim is invented: likejacking hit ordinary people who were signed in to the social network, which is exactly why the hidden Like worked.
os windows
user Dana Okafor
about
  | In 2010 a "shocking video" link in a friend's post led to a page with a big Play button. An invisible Like button sat exactly over it.
  | One click liked the page as you and posted it to your friends, who clicked it too. Then the page asked you to update your video player or do a survey. The update was a toolbar installer that changed the home page.
  | Dana's job in this training is invented: the scam hit ordinary people who were signed in to the social network, not one profession.
story
  | You are Dana Okafor, community assistant at Northwind Traders, a small online shop. Each day you thank customers who post about their orders on Peoplenet, the social network, from your own account.
  | It is early afternoon. You have thanked 8 of today's 10 customer posts. Two to go. You stay signed in to Peoplenet all day.
  | Your Peoplenet details are in a text file on the desktop. That is a bad habit, but it keeps this training quick.
quota 8 10 Customer posts thanked today

# Dana's desk (soft flag: careless, but only here to keep the training simple).
file Desktop/peoplenet-login.txt
  at 930 200
  | Peoplenet (Northwind Traders)
  | User: dana.okafor
  | Password: Teapot-2026!

# The safe task: a customer's post, a Like button you can see, a thank-you.
page liked-9 peoplenet.example/northwind/posts/2291/liked
  title Peoplenet: Liked
  brand Peoplenet
  heading You liked this post
  | Tomas Berg will see: "Dana Okafor likes this."
page skipped-9 peoplenet.example/northwind/posts/2291/skipped
  title Peoplenet: Skipped
  brand Peoplenet
  heading Post skipped
  | You can come back to Tomas Berg's post later.
page post-9 peoplenet.example/northwind/posts/2291
  title Peoplenet: Customer post
  brand Peoplenet
  favorite
  heading Tomas Berg wrote on Northwind Traders
  | "The teapot arrived this morning and it pours perfectly. Thank you, Northwind!"
  | 6 people like this.
  button Like and thank -> liked-9
  button Skip for now -> skipped-9
mail cust-9
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Customer post to thank: Tomas Berg (teapot)
  link post-9
  | Hi Dana,
  |
  | Tomas posted about a teapot on our page. The link goes straight to the post, ready for a Like and a thank-you.
  |
  | Priya

step Customer post 9 of 10
  look Mail: Priya's message with the customer's post
  | A new customer post has come in from Priya, in Customer Service. This one is real. Thank it the normal way, so you know what normal looks like.
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Customer post to thank: Tomas Berg (teapot)

step The link goes to Peoplenet
  look the link under Priya's message
  when mail cust-9
  | The email links to Peoplenet's own address, peoplenet.example. Hover over a link before you click it, to check where it goes.
open cust-9

step A Like you can see
  look the Like and thank button under the post
  when visit post-9
  move Click “Like and thank” under Tomas's post.
  | This is how a Like normally looks: a button with its name on it, in plain sight, on the social network's own page. Remember what it looks like.
open post-9

step Liked and thanked
  look the counter in the guide: one post left
  when choose post-9 any
  | Done. One post to go. Another notification has just arrived: a friend shared something.
choose post-9 1
quota +1

# The lure: a friend's "shocking video" link.
page feed peoplenet.example/home
  title Peoplenet: News feed
  brand Peoplenet
  heading News feed
  | Marcus Lee shared a link: "OMG you won't believe what this girl did [VIDEO]".
  | 14 friends like this. clip-zone.example
  button Watch video
page video clip-zone.example/watch
  title OMG you won't believe what this girl did
  heading Click Play to watch
  | 3:12 · 2,481,903 views
  button Play
  section Hidden layer (shown for training)
  tone warn
  row Visible button = Play
  row Invisible button on top = Like this page
  note The social network's Like button, made see-through and placed over Play.
mail share
  from Peoplenet <notifications@peoplenet.example>
  subject Marcus Lee shared a link
  link feed
  | Marcus Lee shared a link on Peoplenet:
  |
  | "OMG you won't believe what this girl did [VIDEO]"
  |
  | 14 friends like this.
notify mail Peoplenet
  | Marcus Lee shared a link

step A friend's video
  look the post in the feed, and the address under it
  when visit feed
  move Open the message from Peoplenet and click its link.
  | Marcus Lee, a friend, shared a video link. A link from a friend feels safe, but Marcus did not write it. Marcus's account was tricked into sharing it. The headline is bait, and the video is on clip-zone.example, not on Peoplenet.
open feed

step The Play button
  look the big Play button, and the note under it
  when choose feed 1
  move Click “Watch video”.
  | The link opens a page with a video player and one big Play button. The address is no longer Peoplenet's. The picture is only a still image of a player.
open video

step One click
  look the page after you press Play
  when choose video 1
  move Click “Play”.
  | You are signed in to Peoplenet, so your click on Play lands on the invisible Like button over it. The social network posts that you like this link to all your friends. Nothing on screen says so. The video does not play.
# The fake "video player update". Real scams used a program like this; the file is fictional and does nothing.
view clipplayer-setup wizard
  title Clip Player Update
  app Clip Player Update
  publisher ClipCodec Media Ltd
  page Update your video player
  icon program
  | Your video player is out of date, so the video cannot play.
  | Click Next to install the new player.
  button Next -> next primary
  button Cancel -> close
  page Free extras
  icon info
  | Clip Player is free. Our partners help keep it that way.
  section Optional offers
  check [x] Install the Clipfinder toolbar
  check [x] Make Clipfinder my home page and search
  note Recommended
  button Next -> next primary
  button Cancel -> close
  page Finished
  icon shield-bad
  | The new player is installed. Your video will start in a moment.
  button Finish -> done primary
program clipplayer Clip Player Update (clipplayer-update.exe)
  publisher none
  signed no
  prompt open-warning
  description Fake video player update
  process clipcodec.exe
  cpu 2
  mem 21
  parent explorer.exe
  command C:\Users\Dana\AppData\Roaming\ClipCodec\clipcodec.exe
  startup ClipCodecHelper C:\Users\Dana\AppData\Roaming\ClipCodec\clipcodec.exe
  location HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run
  view clipplayer-setup
page survey clip-zone.example/update
  title Player update needed
  heading Your video player is out of date
  | Install the update to watch, or complete a short survey to unlock the video.
  button Download update
  section Survey offer
  row Prize = Free gift card
  row Entry = Your phone number
open survey

step Install the update, or do a survey
  look the page: the player is "out of date"
  when choose survey 1
  move Click “Download update”.
  | The page says your video player is out of date. A real player never asks this on a video page. The update is a program, and the survey wants your phone number.
file Downloads/clipplayer-update.exe
  program clipplayer
  size 311296
open Downloads

step The warning almost nobody reads
  look Publisher "Unknown Publisher", Type "Application"
  when prompt clipplayer
  move Double-click “clipplayer-update” in Downloads.
  | A video player update is a program from an unknown publisher. Your computer wants to know whether to run it. Most people clicked Run to see their video.
open Downloads/clipplayer-update.exe

step The setup, with two offers
  look the setup window: Next, then the page with the two offers
  when run clipplayer
  cue view-btn:next view-btn:done view:clipplayer-setup
  move Click Next on each page until Finish.
  | The "update" plays no video. Its installer adds a toolbar and sets a new home page. It also adds a start-up entry, so it runs every time the computer starts.
answer run

